    "result_text": "Tests remain green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I addressed\n\n**Finding 1 (duplicated SHA-256 \u2192 upper-hex) \u2014 agreed and fixed.** It was a correct catch: `generateHouseholdId` still carried its own `MessageDigest`/`%02X`-loop/`NoSuchAlgorithmException` block, byte-for-byte the same as the new `sha256UpperHex` helper. I collapsed it to route through the helper:\n\n```java\nprivate static String generateHouseholdId(String lastName, String address) {\n    return \"HH-\" + sha256UpperHex(lastName + \"\\u0000\" + address, 12);\n}\n```\n\nThere's now a single digest-to-hex implementation. Behaviour is unchanged: the old loop took the first 6 bytes as `%02X` (12 upper-hex chars), which is exactly `sha256UpperHex(..., 12)` \u2014 same casing, same length, same `\"HH-\"` prefix. The `MessageDigest`/`NoSuchAlgorithmException`/`StandardCharsets` imports are still needed by the helper, so nothing became unused.\n\n**Finding 2 (split layout knowledge) \u2014 agreed it's worth a cross-link, kept the placement.** As the reviewer noted, `Region` legitimately owns region identity, so I left `regionOfCustomerCode` where it is and just added reciprocal \"keep the two in sync\" pointers between it and `generateCustomerCode` so the coupling is discoverable from either side.\n\nAll acceptance behaviour is intact.",
